      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the typical pH range for an industrial degreaser?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Industrial degreasers designed to remove mineral oils, synthetic cutting fluids, and machine greases typically operate in the pH range of 9 to 13. This alkaline window enables two concurrent mechanisms: saponification of any ester-based oils present (converting them to water-soluble soaps and glycerol) and emulsification of non-saponifiable hydrocarbons via nonionic and anionic surfactant systems. The precise pH is determined by the substrate sensitivity, with lower values preferred for aluminium and zinc alloys, which are vulnerable to corrosive attack at pH above 11." }
